        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: به شرط اینکه",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به شرط اینکه (be shart-e inke) — \"provided that, on condition that\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "میآیم، به شرط اینکه زود برگردیم. miâyam, be shart-e inke zud bargardim. I will come, provided that we come back early."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes the subjunctive: be shart-e inke + bargardim. With a noun: be shart-e …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به شرط اینکه (be shart-e inke) is literally \"on the condition that\": shart was borrowed from Arabic sharṭ \"condition\" (EtymDB), and be \"to\" and inke \"that\" (in \"this\" + ke \"that\") are Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
