              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در صورتی که (dar surati ke) — \"in the event that, if\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در صورتی که باران بیاید، در خانه میمانیم. dar surati ke bârân biyâyad, dar khâne mimânim. If it rains, we will stay at home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes the subjunctive, like agar, and sounds more formal. With the indicative it can also mean \"whereas\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در صورتی که (dar surati ke) is literally \"in a form that\": surat comes from Arabic ṣūra \"form, image\" (EtymDB), here a state of affairs, and dar \"in\" and ke \"that\" are Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
